simplicity: remove dead state, eliminate shadowing, add NodeState sync guard, replace ForEach map with typed binding (#185)

## Summary

Four simplicity fixes from a reconciling-implementations audit against
the designs:

- **Remove dead field `reconcileState.nodeCount`** — set but never read
by any status derivation function
- **Eliminate `hasPerItemGate` shadowing** — same invariant expression
re-declared inside forEach loop; hoisted to outer scope
- **Add NodeState/nodeStateLabels sync guard** — `_nodeStateCount`
sentinel + `init()` assertion panics at startup if a new state is added
without updating metric labels
- **Replace `ForEach map[string]string` with `*ForEachBinding` struct**
— the design says multi-variable cross-product is unsupported; the map
permitted multiple keys with a runtime guard; the struct encodes the
single-dimension constraint at the type level. Parser still accepts both
YAML shapes.

All presubmit (unit + e2e + compat) pass.
